Feature: Channel-wise Biosimilar Sales Performance Analysis

  This feature analyzes the sales performance of biosimilar brands (kanjinti, mvasi, riabni) across different channels (online, retail, mobile) using the purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack table. The analysis aggregates sales metrics (integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, integrated_dollars) within a 36-month window from cdl_effective_date, grouped by brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, and channel_name.

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the source table is "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack"
    And the analysis is limited to brands "kanjinti", "mvasi", and "riabni"
    And the sales metrics to be aggregated are "integrated_units", "integrated_normalized_units", and "integrated_dollars"
    And the grouping attributes are "brand_normalized_name", "normalized_name", "market_normalized_name", "competitor_flag", and "channel_name"
    And the time filter is applied using "cdl_effective_date"
    And only records with valid, non-null "cdl_effective_date" in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD) are included
    And the 36-month window is calculated as records where "transaction_timestamp" >= "cdl_effective_date" AND "transaction_timestamp" < "cdl_effective_date" + INTERVAL 36 MONTH

  Scenario: Happy path - Valid biosimilar sales aggregation by channel
    Given the table contains records for brands "kanjinti", "mvasi", and "riabni"
    And all records have valid "cdl_effective_date" in "YYYY-MM-DD" format
    And "transaction_timestamp" is within 36 months from "cdl_effective_date"
    When the data is filtered by brand and time window
    And grouped by "brand_normalized_name", "normalized_name", "market_normalized_name", "competitor_flag", "channel_name"
    And sales metrics are aggregated by sum for each group
    Then the output contains the total "integrated_units", "integrated_normalized_units", and "integrated_dollars" for each channel
    And the output format is a grouped table

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - Invalid or null cdl_effective_date handling
    Given the table contains records for brands "<brand_normalized_name>"
    And the "cdl_effective_date" value is "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When the data is filtered for valid "cdl_effective_date"
    Then records with invalid or null "cdl_effective_date" are excluded from the analysis
    And an error log is generated in "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log" with error_message "<error_message>"

    Examples:
      | brand_normalized_name | cdl_effective_date | error_message                                 |
      | kanjinti             | null               | "cdl_effective_date is null"                   |
      | mvasi                | "2022-13-01"       | "cdl_effective_date format invalid"            |
      | riabni               | "2021/05/10"       | "cdl_effective_date format invalid"            |
      | kanjinti             | ""                 | "cdl_effective_date is empty"                  |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - Transaction timestamp outside 36-month window
    Given the table contains a record for brand "<brand_normalized_name>" with "cdl_effective_date" "<cdl_effective_date>" and "transaction_timestamp" "<transaction_timestamp>"
    When the time window filter is applied
    Then the record is excluded from the analysis
    And an error log is generated in "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log" with error_message "transaction_timestamp outside 36-month window"

    Examples:
      | brand_normalized_name | cdl_effective_date | transaction_timestamp    |
      | mvasi                | "2021-01-01"       | "2024-02-02 00:00:00"   |
      | riabni               | "2020-06-15"       | "2023-07-16 12:00:00"   |

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven channel-wise aggregation
    Given the table contains valid records for brand "<brand_normalized_name>" in channel "<channel_name>" with "cdl_effective_date" "<cdl_effective_date>" and "transaction_timestamp" "<transaction_timestamp>"
    When the data is filtered and grouped as specified
    Then the output contains the sum of "integrated_units", "integrated_normalized_units", and "integrated_dollars" for each group

    Examples:
      | brand_normalized_name | channel_name | cdl_effective_date | transaction_timestamp    | integrated_units | integrated_normalized_units | integrated_dollars |
      | kanjinti             | online       | "2022-01-01"       | "2022-05-01 10:00:00"   | 1000            | 950                        | 120000             |
      | mvasi                | retail       | "2021-06-15"       | "2022-06-20 09:00:00"   | 800             | 780                        | 95000              |
      | riabni               | mobile       | "2023-03-10"       | "2023-08-12 15:00:00"   | 500             | 480                        | 60000              |

  Scenario: Error scenario - No valid records after filtering
    Given the table contains only records with invalid or null "cdl_effective_date"
    When the data is filtered for valid "cdl_effective_date" and time window
    Then the output is an empty table
    And an error message "No valid records found for analysis" is logged

  Scenario: Output format specification
    Given the analysis is complete
    When the output is generated
    Then the output is a grouped table with columns:
      | brand_normalized_name | normalized_name | market_normalized_name | competitor_flag | channel_name | sum_integrated_units | sum_integrated_normalized_units | sum_integrated_dollars |
    And the output is delivered in CSV format

  Scenario: Table selection validation
    Given the analysis requirements
    When the source table is selected
    Then only "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack" is used for aggregation
    And other tables (e.g., *_weekly, *_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log) are used only for error logging or validation, not for aggregation

  Scenario: Validation rule - cdl_effective_date format
    Given a record with "cdl_effective_date" value
    When the value is parsed
    Then it must match the ISO 8601 format "YYYY-MM-DD"
    And if not, the record is excluded and error logged

  Scenario: Validation rule - competitor_flag
    Given a record with "competitor_flag" value
    When the value is parsed
    Then it must be boolean (true or false)
    And if not, the record is excluded and error logged

  Scenario: Validation rule - channel_name
    Given a record with "channel_name" value
    When the value is parsed
    Then it must be one of "online", "retail", "mobile"
    And if not, the record is excluded and error logged

